  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "On November 23, 2026, the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) of Indonesia expected President Prabowo Subianto to submit the names of two candidates for the position of vice president. This follows the reported need to appoint a successor for Gibran. MPR Speaker Ahmad Muzani confirmed that the institution has been conducting joint meetings and official correspondence to remind the administration of the deadline for this submission. While the exact timing for the delivery of the letters remained fluid, the process has drawn significant public and political attention as the date coincides with the final window for the transition. Several political leaders, including Golkar Chairman Bahlil Lahadalia, have expressed that they are leaving the determination of the candidates entirely to the president's discretion. The parliament building in Senayan, Jakarta, has been prepared for the anticipated arrival of the president's formal proposal.",
